<task id="122" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>H0.5: DI-swap onto C1.4 registry client (remove NullDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient)</title>
    <phase>C'' Wave G-2 -- Entry + resources</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Re-activates FR-02 re-consent semantics that are currently inert (PARTIAL per DS-4) -- correctness-relevant for the H0.5 consent-capture path; touches BFF-adjacent onboarding semantics (though the swap is L2-side).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Small DI-swap (~50 LOC per DS-4) with well-defined branch tests -- Sonnet @ high.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>112</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, job-handler, path-x</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>DI-swap H0.5's registry-client dependency from NullDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient (which always returns null, making FR-02 re-consent semantics currently inert per DS-4 §2 H0.5 row -- 'core real, idempotency/restart-vs-no-op logic correct, but NullDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient always returns null') onto task 112's real IDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient implementation. Verify the re-consent no-op vs restart branches now correctly read actual registry state.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in DI-swap verification and idempotency-branch testing against a now-real dependency.</role>

  <goal>H0.5's owning module registers the real IDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient (task 112) in place of the Null-Object. The existing re-consent no-op vs restart branch logic (already correct per DS-4) now operates against REAL registry data from a fake registry populated with test data, proving the previously-inert FR-02 semantics are live.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-4 §2 (H0.5 row) and §3 confirm: H0.5's core handler logic (idempotency, restart-vs-no-op branching) is ALREADY CORRECT -- the only gap is that its registry-client dependency is a Null-Object returning null unconditionally, making the correct branching logic operate on fictional (always-empty) data. This is the smallest task in Wave G-2 (~50 LOC) precisely because the hard work (task 112's client + task 111's grant) already landed in Wave G-1.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/ConsentCapture/H05ConsentCaptureHandler.cs (or its owning module -- DI registration only)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Registry/DataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="112" status="pending">The real registry client this task swaps onto must exist</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-38">L2's admin-env Dataverse credential model is Path X: L2 UAMI registered as a Dataverse Application User via DefaultAzureCredential pinned to the UAMI (DS-8). MUST NOT provision a new client-secret for L2. The Dataverse-ClientSecret KV secret itself MUST NOT be deleted (BFF still consumes it) -- only L2's dependency on it is removed.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>H0.5 registry client DI-swap</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read H05ConsentCaptureHandler.cs's registry-client consumption + its existing idempotency branch tests.</step>
    <step order="1" name="DI swap">Replace the NullDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient registration with DataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient in H0.5's owning module.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Verify branches">Run/extend the existing re-consent no-op vs restart branch tests against a fake IDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient populated with data (proving the branching logic, already correct, now has real data to branch on).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Integration smoke">Against dev spaarkedev1 (post task 111 grant), verify an actual H0.5 invocation reads a real registry row's re-consent state correctly.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Build + verify">dotnet build 0 errors; dotnet test green.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build/test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">H0.5 owning module DI registration (modified)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'NullDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient' in H0.5's active DI registration returns 0 matches.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Existing re-consent no-op vs restart branch tests pass against a data-populated fake registry client (not the Null-Object).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Integration smoke test (dev, post task 111) confirms a real registry read succeeds under the H0.5 handler's invocation path.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- H0.5's branch logic is already correct; only the data source is fictional. Extension -- swapping the DI registration is the direct, minimal fix; no redesign needed. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- FR-02 re-consent semantics stay permanently inert regardless of how correct the branch logic is.</notes>

